4,0 $ Veil pale, whitish, cream or ochre; spores distinctly mitriform $ C. micaceus
5,0$ Basidiocarps medium-sized, somewhat fleshy, pale ochre, rust or cinnamon; stipe 3-10 mm wide; veil made up of very small, scattered, granular flocks, not covering entire pileus when young, microscopically of (sub)globose, hyalin, thin-walled cells, not in chains; pileus subglobose to ovoid, only tardily expanding to campanulate$subsect. Micacei (Fr.) Uljé & Noordel.).$s"ss.micacei"

