Rem -->COPRINUS SUBSECTION DOMESTICI
Rem -->-->Basidiocarps medium-sized, somewhat fleshy, pale ochre to ochre; stipe 3-10 mm wide; veil covering entire pileus when young, breaking up of small, woolly flocks (in C. bipellis in patches), microscopically of chains of cylindrical, ellipsoid, broadly fusiform or (sub)globose, hyalin, thin-walled and in part thick-walled and yellow-brown cells; terminal cells distinct, cylindrical, ellipsoid, ovoid or fusiform; pileus subglobose to ovoid, only tardily expanding to campanulate (subsect. Domestici Sing.).KEY TO THE SPECIES
1,5$ Type
1,0 $ Spores ellipsoid, up to 16 µm long; germ pore eccentric $ C. flocculosus
1,2 $ . Spores cylindric-ellipsoid, up to 12(-13) µm long; germ pore central.
2,0 $ Spore length up to 12(-13) µm long $ C. radians
2,3 $ . Spore length less than 10(-11) µm.
3,0 $ Veil breaking up in patches (like in Amanita) $ C. bipellis
3,4 $ . Veil breaking up in small, woolly flocks (up to 2 mm diam.).
4,0 $ Spore breadth up to 4.5 µm; pileus 25-40 x 20-30 mm before expanding; usually on and around truncs $ C. domesticus
4,0 $ Spore breadth 4.5-5.5 µm; pileus 20-30 x 15-20 mm before expanding; usually on dead branches $ C. xanthothrix
5,0$Basidiocarps medium-sized, somewhat fleshy, pale ochre to ochre; stipe 3-10 mm wide; veil covering entire pileus when young, breaking up of small, woolly flocks (in C. bipellis in patches), microscopically of chains of cylindrical, ellipsoid, broadly fusiform or (sub)globose, hyalin, thin-walled and in part thick-walled and yellow-brown cells; terminal cells distinct, cylindrical, ellipsoid, ovoid or fusiform; pileus subglobose to ovoid, only tardily expanding to campanulate $subsect. Domestici Sing.).$s"domestici"


