2,0 $ Basidia 2-spored; pileus grey or cream-grey, sometimes white at first: $ C. pachyspermus
2,3 $ . Basidia 4-spored; pileus white at first
3,0 $ Spores 10--15 x 6.5--8.5 µm; spores ± 6-angular (hexagonal); pleurocystidia absent or very sparse: $ C. cothurnatus
3,0 $ Spores 12--19 x 11--15.5 µm; spores ± limoniform; pleurocystidia present: $ C. niveus
4,5 $ . Spores oval or ellipsoid, sometimes slightly cylindrical
4,15 $ . Spores differently shaped
5,0 $ Basidia 2-spored: $ C. bellulus
5,6 $ . Basidia 4-spored
6,0 $ Cystidia absent: $ C. cortinatus
6,7 $ . Cystidia present
7,8 $ . Both cheilo- en pleurocystidia present
7,13 $ . Only cheilocystidia present
8,9 $ . Pileus very small, expanded < 6 mm; average length of spores < 9 µm
8,11 $ . Pileus larger, 5--25 mm when expanded or av. length of spores > 9 µm
9,0 $ In lawns, terrestrial, not on dung, young pileus white; spores 7--9.5 x 5--6.5 µm: $ C. idae
9,10 $ . On dung; pileus grey or white and then breadth of spores < 5 µm
10,0 $ Young pileus grey; spores 7.5--9.5 x 5--6 µm: $ C. poliomallus
10,0 $ Young pileus white; spores 6--7.5(--8) x 3.5--4.5(--5) µm: $ C. pseudocortinatus
11,0 $ Expanded pileus up to 25 mm; av. length of spores < 9 µm; on dung: $ C. utrifer
11,12 $ . Expanded pileus 5--12 mm; av. length of spores > 9 µm
12,0 $ On grasses. Cheilocystidia 20--45 x 8--13 µm: $ C. pilosotomentosus
12,0 $ On wood. Cheilocystidia 50--80 x 20--35 µm: $ C. nemoralis
13,0 $ Cheilocystidia utriform: $ C. candidatus
13,14 $ . Cheilocystidia (sub)globose or ellipsoid
14,0 $ Caulocystidia absent, cheilocystidia without diverticulations in apical part: see discussion under $ C. cortinatus
14,0 $ Caulocystidia present, with finger-like diverculations at apex; cheilocystidia (sub)globose to ellipsoid, partly also diverculate: $ C. ramosocystidiatus
15,16 $ . Spores with rounded angles (4--5-angular), 8--10.5 x 8--10 µm; pleurocystidia present
15,18 $ . Spores differently shaped; breadth of spores < 8 µm or spores limoniform; pleurocystidia present or absent
16,0 $ Ring present: $ C. ephemeroides
16,17 $ . Ring absent
17,0 $ Cheilocystidia in part lageniform. On dung: $ C. cordisporus
17,0 $ No lageniform cheilocystidia present. On vegetable debris: $ C. patouillardii
18,19 $ . Pleurocystidia present
18,20 $ . Pleurocystidia absent
19,0 $ Breadth of spores 5--6 µm, heart- or pear-shaped: $ C. cardiasporus
19,0 $ Breadth of spores 7.5--11.5 µm, limoniform: $ C. pseudoniveus
20,0 $ Veil at centre of pileus dark grey, usually with greenish hue; spores narrowly ovoid or amygdaliform, c. 4--5 µm broad: $ C. coniophorus
20,0 $ Veil white, often cream-coloured or slightly ochraceous at centre of pileus; spores ± 6-angular in frontal view, c. 5--6 µm broad; with two bumps at each side: $ C. iocularis

